${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=1.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186395049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395046 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "659dcf86-3da2-503b-9a49-309b10754236" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395047 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186395047 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395047 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e2ad9ead-87b5-5eaf-8e9e-875db0473a7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395048 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186395048 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395048 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dfc2aec0-03c1-52f2-822c-b5b8cc4452d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395049 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 175921